  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "Define \\(x \\otimes y = x^3 - y.\\) What is \\(h \\otimes (h \\otimes h)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-h\\)",
    "B": "\\(0\\)",
    "C": "\\(h\\)",
    "D": "\\(2h\\)",
    "E": "\\(h^3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First apply the definition to the operation inside parentheses:\n\\[\nh\\otimes h=h^3-h.\n\\]\nIn the outer operation, the first input is still \\(h\\), and the entire second input is \\(h^3-h\\). Therefore\n\\[\nh\\otimes(h\\otimes h)=h^3-(h^3-h)=h^3-h^3+h=h.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{h}\\), choice C.",
